{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RhcaBcAu9ZTsCUFHRWG9F2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n2\t\n3\t> Revised 2026-05-19 after Dream review (best case = 2.5/5). Major reframing: drop \"paradox\" narrative, engage related work, add retrieval benchmarks.\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR)\n7\t- Stretch: EMNLP 2026 Main\n8\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n9\t\n10\t## Paper Type\n11\tEmpirical analysis paper — quantifying a known phenomenon (per-example divergence under aggregate convergence) in a specific important domain (hybrid recurrent architectures)\n12\t\n13\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n14\t\n15\t### Claim 1: Task-Dependent Convergence\n16\tAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength varies with task type. Convergence is strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233, underpowered at n=5), and absent on reasoning-heavy tasks. **Critical need**: a second high-retrieval benchmark showing significant convergence to survive multi-comparison correction.\n17\t\n18\t### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\n19\tThe convergence effect requires sufficient model capacity: monotonically complete at 1.3B (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound. Only two scale points (Wang et al. cap at 1.3B). Frame as binary contrast, not extrapolatable trend.\n20\t\n21\t### Claim 3: Per-Example Divergence Under Aggregate Convergence\n22\tDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on nearly non-overlapping sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). This is an instance of the well-documented underspecification phenomenon (D'Amour et al. 2022) applied to hybrid architectures. Our contribution is **quantifying** it in this specific context, NOT claiming to discover it. Surface features AND baseline model perplexity do not differentiate helped/hurt samples within an architecture — the effect is opaque to standard features. However, cross-architecture comparison reveals systematic differences in baseline difficulty profiles of affected samples (Kruskal-Wallis p=0.0005 for hurt samples), confirming the architecture-specificity is structured, not random noise.\n23\t\n24\t## Story Spine\n25\t\n26\t### Problem\n27\tHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming standard. While Wang et al. (2025) provide an extensive model zoo, the community lacks quantitative understanding of how attention affects cross-architecture behavioral diversity at the per-example level.\n28\t\n29\t### Related Work Positioning (CRITICAL — Dream W2)\n30\tThe observation that models with similar aggregate performance differ per-example is well-established:\n31\t- **Ensemble diversity**: Krogh & Vedelsby (1995), Kuncheva & Whitaker (2003) — diverse ensemble members err on different examples by construction\n32\t- **Underspecification**: D'Amour et al. (2022) — equivalent aggregate performance masks prediction-level differences\n33\t- **Dataset cartography**: Swayamdipta et al. (2020) — per-example difficulty varies across models\n34\t- **Simpson's paradox / ecological fallacy**: Aggregate-vs-disaggregate discrepancy is a textbook phenomenon\n35\t\n36\tOur contribution is NOT discovering this phenomenon. It IS quantifying how it manifests specifically when attention is added to linear recurrent models, and characterizing its task-dependency and scale-dependency. This is valuable because hybrid architectures are a design choice practitioners make — understanding per-example implications informs that choice.\n37\t\n38\t### Our Framing\n39\tWe provide the first systematic per-example analysis of attention's equalizing effect in hybrid recurrent architectures. Using Wang et al.'s public model zoo (72 models), we quantify (a) task-dependent convergence strength, (b) scale-dependent convergence completeness, and (c) architecture-specific per-example divergence patterns. Our contribution is analytical depth on public infrastructure, not new methods or models.\n40\t\n41\t### Headline Result Template\n42\t\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention to hybrid recurrent models reduces cross-architecture variance by 79% on LAMBADA, yet per-example analysis reveals nearly non-overlapping affected sample subsets (Jaccard < 0.10) — a manifestation of underspecification that has practical implications for architecture selection.\"\n43\t\n44\t## Dream Review Findings (D006) — Must Address\n45\t\n46\t### W1: Single-benchmark significance [MAJOR, blocking]\n47\tAfter Bonferroni (6 benchmarks, α=0.0083), LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed) does NOT survive. Need: (a) FDR correction (Benjamini-Hochberg) as primary reporting, (b) additional high-retrieval benchmarks for a second significant anchor. Candidates: StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA, closed-book QA tasks available in lm-eval.\n48\t\n49\t### W2: Missing related work [MAJOR, blocking for submission]\n50\tNeed 20+ references engaging ensemble diversity, underspecification, dataset cartography, attention interpretability, hybrid architectures (Jamba, RWKV-6, RecurrentGemma). Paper Agent handles this during writing.\n51\t\n52\t### W3: Mechanistic overclaiming [MAJOR, partially addressed]\n53\tAlready reworded Claim 3 from \"Mechanism\" to \"Effects\". Must NOT use \"mechanistic analysis\" in paper — use \"characterization\" or \"decomposition\" instead. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive, not causal. Frame honestly.\n54\t\n55\t### W4: Incremental over Wang et al. [MAJOR]\n56\tMitigate by: (a) engaging related work to show the QUESTION we ask is independently motivated by ensemble/underspecification literature, (b) framing contribution as analytical toolkit + quantitative characterization, not re-analysis. (c) Per-example analysis is genuinely novel for this model family.\n57\t\n58\t## Venue Fit Risks\n59\t(unchanged from previous version, see git history)\n60\t\n61\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n62\t\n63\t### Concern A: \"This is just a re-analysis of Wang et al.'s models\"\n64\tResponse: Yes, and that's the point — public infrastructure enables community analysis. Our per-example decomposition, task-dependency characterization, and scale-dependency analysis are not in Wang et al. The contribution is analytical, like meta-analyses in medicine.\n65\tRequired: Strong Related Work positioning; frame as \"community analysis\" paper.\n66\t\n67\t### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Bonferroni failure\n68\t**Statistical strategy** (from exp-008, verified by Reviewer with independent reproduction):\n69\t1. **Lead with percentile CI (valid-only)**: BCa degenerates at ρ=-1.0 boundary (z0=-3.86); fall back to percentile CI on valid bootstrap resamples (8875/10000; 11.25% degenerate from n=3 same-architecture redraws). Valid-only percentile CI = **[-1.0, -0.7]**, 100% of valid resamples have ρ<0. Full percentile CI (degenerate-as-zero) = [-1.0, 0.0] touches zero. Paper leads with valid-only CI; BCa degeneracy + degenerate-sample treatment in appendix.\n70\t2. **Report exact permutation p**: LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed, 2/120 permutations). Honest and transparent.\n71\t3. **Bonferroni in supplementary**: adj-p=0.100 (two-tailed). Report honestly as \"does not survive Bonferroni.\" BH-FDR also gives 0.100 (no additional benefit with only 1 small p-value). If exp-011 produces a second significant benchmark, BH-FDR becomes more favorable than Bonferroni.\n72\t4. **GDN-excluded sensitivity**: Excluding GDN (D004 confound): LAMBADA ρ drops to -0.7 (p=0.233); ARC-Easy ρ **improves** from -0.7 to -0.9 (p=0.083, suggestive — D004 noise removed); **⚠️ MMLU ρ FLIPS from -0.7 to +0.6** — MMLU apparent convergence was entirely GDN-driven and MUST NOT appear as convergence evidence anywhere in the paper (D007). Report both full and GDN-excluded analyses. The ARC-Easy improvement after confound removal is itself informative, especially in exp-011 context.\n73\t5. **exp-011**: Additional retrieval benchmarks (StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA) for a potential second significant anchor. CRITICAL for acceptance — with exp-011 data, BH-FDR could diverge favorably from Bonferroni.\n74\t6. **Effect sizes**: Cohen's d CI crosses zero; omega² near zero. Do NOT lead with effect sizes — lead with BCa CI and convergence magnitude (std 0.024→0.005, 79% reduction).\n75\t\n76\tRequired experiments: exp-011 (additional retrieval benchmarks), exp-008 (robustness with corrected p-values), exp-002 (per-example validation).\n77\t\n78\t### Concern C: \"The per-example divergence is a known phenomenon\"\n79\tResponse: Acknowledge explicitly. Our contribution is quantification in hybrid architectures, not discovery of the phenomenon. Cite ensemble diversity + underspecification.\n80\tRequired: Related Work section (Paper Agent).\n81\t\n82\t### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\n83\tResponse: 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. Per-example analysis provides 5153 data points per comparison. Check for additional architectures (exp-005).\n84\t\n85\t### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\n86\tResponse: Binary contrast, not trend. 7B unavailable. Frame as \"scale is a necessary condition.\" exp-007 for 340M rebound mechanism.\n87\t\n88\t### Concern F: \"No causal mechanism\" (NEW from Dream)\n89\tResponse: We do NOT claim causal mechanism. We characterize and describe. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive. Interventional experiments (head swaps, ablations) are acknowledged as future work. Honest framing prevents overclaiming.\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96a4463a-edfa-429d-98c4-89aa467fd2ef","uuid":"04876e13-1053-4809-b1b6-bafe49d861de","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:16:47.885Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — entrainment_gated_ft\n\n> Revised 2026-05-19 after Dream review (best case = 2.5/5). Major reframing: drop \"paradox\" narrative, engage related work, add retrieval benchmarks.\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR)\n- Stretch: EMNLP 2026 Main\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis paper — quantifying a known phenomenon (per-example divergence under aggregate convergence) in a specific important domain (hybrid recurrent architectures)\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n### Claim 1: Task-Dependent Convergence\nAdding attention layers to different linear recurrent architectures (GatedDeltaNet, RetNet, HGRN2) induces aggregate performance convergence whose strength varies with task type. Convergence is strongest on LAMBADA (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed, cross-arch std drops 79%), suggestive on ARC-Easy (ρ=-0.7, p=0.233, underpowered at n=5), and absent on reasoning-heavy tasks. **Critical need**: a second high-retrieval benchmark showing significant convergence to survive multi-comparison correction.\n\n### Claim 2: Scale-Dependent Convergence\nThe convergence effect requires sufficient model capacity: monotonically complete at 1.3B (ρ=-1.0, p=0.017 two-tailed) but only partial at 340M with a non-monotonic rebound. Only two scale points (Wang et al. cap at 1.3B). Frame as binary contrast, not extrapolatable trend.\n\n### Claim 3: Per-Example Divergence Under Aggregate Convergence\nDespite aggregate convergence, attention acts on nearly non-overlapping sample subsets per architecture (pairwise Jaccard < 0.10). This is an instance of the well-documented underspecification phenomenon (D'Amour et al. 2022) applied to hybrid architectures. Our contribution is **quantifying** it in this specific context, NOT claiming to discover it. Surface features AND baseline model perplexity do not differentiate helped/hurt samples within an architecture — the effect is opaque to standard features. However, cross-architecture comparison reveals systematic differences in baseline difficulty profiles of affected samples (Kruskal-Wallis p=0.0005 for hurt samples), confirming the architecture-specificity is structured, not random noise.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nHybrid architectures mixing linear recurrence with full attention are becoming standard. While Wang et al. (2025) provide an extensive model zoo, the community lacks quantitative understanding of how attention affects cross-architecture behavioral diversity at the per-example level.\n\n### Related Work Positioning (CRITICAL — Dream W2)\nThe observation that models with similar aggregate performance differ per-example is well-established:\n- **Ensemble diversity**: Krogh & Vedelsby (1995), Kuncheva & Whitaker (2003) — diverse ensemble members err on different examples by construction\n- **Underspecification**: D'Amour et al. (2022) — equivalent aggregate performance masks prediction-level differences\n- **Dataset cartography**: Swayamdipta et al. (2020) — per-example difficulty varies across models\n- **Simpson's paradox / ecological fallacy**: Aggregate-vs-disaggregate discrepancy is a textbook phenomenon\n\nOur contribution is NOT discovering this phenomenon. It IS quantifying how it manifests specifically when attention is added to linear recurrent models, and characterizing its task-dependency and scale-dependency. This is valuable because hybrid architectures are a design choice practitioners make — understanding per-example implications informs that choice.\n\n### Our Framing\nWe provide the first systematic per-example analysis of attention's equalizing effect in hybrid recurrent architectures. Using Wang et al.'s public model zoo (72 models), we quantify (a) task-dependent convergence strength, (b) scale-dependent convergence completeness, and (c) architecture-specific per-example divergence patterns. Our contribution is analytical depth on public infrastructure, not new methods or models.\n\n### Headline Result Template\n\"At 1.3B scale, adding attention to hybrid recurrent models reduces cross-architecture variance by 79% on LAMBADA, yet per-example analysis reveals nearly non-overlapping affected sample subsets (Jaccard < 0.10) — a manifestation of underspecification that has practical implications for architecture selection.\"\n\n## Dream Review Findings (D006) — Must Address\n\n### W1: Single-benchmark significance [MAJOR, blocking]\nAfter Bonferroni (6 benchmarks, α=0.0083), LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed) does NOT survive. Need: (a) FDR correction (Benjamini-Hochberg) as primary reporting, (b) additional high-retrieval benchmarks for a second significant anchor. Candidates: StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA, closed-book QA tasks available in lm-eval.\n\n### W2: Missing related work [MAJOR, blocking for submission]\nNeed 20+ references engaging ensemble diversity, underspecification, dataset cartography, attention interpretability, hybrid architectures (Jamba, RWKV-6, RecurrentGemma). Paper Agent handles this during writing.\n\n### W3: Mechanistic overclaiming [MAJOR, partially addressed]\nAlready reworded Claim 3 from \"Mechanism\" to \"Effects\". Must NOT use \"mechanistic analysis\" in paper — use \"characterization\" or \"decomposition\" instead. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive, not causal. Frame honestly.\n\n### W4: Incremental over Wang et al. [MAJOR]\nMitigate by: (a) engaging related work to show the QUESTION we ask is independently motivated by ensemble/underspecification literature, (b) framing contribution as analytical toolkit + quantitative characterization, not re-analysis. (c) Per-example analysis is genuinely novel for this model family.\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n(unchanged from previous version, see git history)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### Concern A: \"This is just a re-analysis of Wang et al.'s models\"\nResponse: Yes, and that's the point — public infrastructure enables community analysis. Our per-example decomposition, task-dependency characterization, and scale-dependency analysis are not in Wang et al. The contribution is analytical, like meta-analyses in medicine.\nRequired: Strong Related Work positioning; frame as \"community analysis\" paper.\n\n### Concern B: \"Only one task shows the effect\" + Bonferroni failure\n**Statistical strategy** (from exp-008, verified by Reviewer with independent reproduction):\n1. **Lead with percentile CI (valid-only)**: BCa degenerates at ρ=-1.0 boundary (z0=-3.86); fall back to percentile CI on valid bootstrap resamples (8875/10000; 11.25% degenerate from n=3 same-architecture redraws). Valid-only percentile CI = **[-1.0, -0.7]**, 100% of valid resamples have ρ<0. Full percentile CI (degenerate-as-zero) = [-1.0, 0.0] touches zero. Paper leads with valid-only CI; BCa degeneracy + degenerate-sample treatment in appendix.\n2. **Report exact permutation p**: LAMBADA p=0.017 (two-tailed, 2/120 permutations). Honest and transparent.\n3. **Bonferroni in supplementary**: adj-p=0.100 (two-tailed). Report honestly as \"does not survive Bonferroni.\" BH-FDR also gives 0.100 (no additional benefit with only 1 small p-value). If exp-011 produces a second significant benchmark, BH-FDR becomes more favorable than Bonferroni.\n4. **GDN-excluded sensitivity**: Excluding GDN (D004 confound): LAMBADA ρ drops to -0.7 (p=0.233); ARC-Easy ρ **improves** from -0.7 to -0.9 (p=0.083, suggestive — D004 noise removed); **⚠️ MMLU ρ FLIPS from -0.7 to +0.6** — MMLU apparent convergence was entirely GDN-driven and MUST NOT appear as convergence evidence anywhere in the paper (D007). Report both full and GDN-excluded analyses. The ARC-Easy improvement after confound removal is itself informative, especially in exp-011 context.\n5. **exp-011**: Additional retrieval benchmarks (StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA) for a potential second significant anchor. CRITICAL for acceptance — with exp-011 data, BH-FDR could diverge favorably from Bonferroni.\n6. **Effect sizes**: Cohen's d CI crosses zero; omega² near zero. Do NOT lead with effect sizes — lead with BCa CI and convergence magnitude (std 0.024→0.005, 79% reduction).\n\nRequired experiments: exp-011 (additional retrieval benchmarks), exp-008 (robustness with corrected p-values), exp-002 (per-example validation).\n\n### Concern C: \"The per-example divergence is a known phenomenon\"\nResponse: Acknowledge explicitly. Our contribution is quantification in hybrid architectures, not discovery of the phenomenon. Cite ensemble diversity + underspecification.\nRequired: Related Work section (Paper Agent).\n\n### Concern D: \"n=3 architectures is too few\"\nResponse: 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models. Per-example analysis provides 5153 data points per comparison. Check for additional architectures (exp-005).\n\n### Concern E: \"Two scales don't establish a trend\"\nResponse: Binary contrast, not trend. 7B unavailable. Frame as \"scale is a necessary condition.\" exp-007 for 340M rebound mechanism.\n\n### Concern F: \"No causal mechanism\" (NEW from Dream)\nResponse: We do NOT claim causal mechanism. We characterize and describe. Attention weight analysis (exp-004) is descriptive. Interventional experiments (head swaps, ablations) are acknowledged as future work. Honest framing prevents overclaiming.\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E3gCsUpki4S7Zbe8KN2vn6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis (task-specificity validation)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Re-run lm-eval on 1.3B models with --log_samples for HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge。收集 per-example logprob 数据。在 worst 档下，这些 reasoning-heavy benchmarks 的 per-example 分析不会产生 convergence 信号， 但会为 per-example divergence 分析提供对比组。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_mean\": 0.08,\n7\t      \"hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_range\": [\n8\t        0.05,\n9\t        0.11\n10\t      ],\n11\t      \"arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_mean\": 0.09,\n12\t      \"arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_range\": [\n13\t        0.06,\n14\t        0.12\n15\t      ],\n16\t      \"arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_mean\": 0.07,\n17\t      \"arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_range\": [\n18\t        0.04,\n19\t        0.1\n20\t      ],\n21\t      \"hellaswag_cross_arch_std_trend_rho\": 0.2,\n22\t      \"hellaswag_cross_arch_std_trend_p\": 0.75,\n23\t      \"arc_easy_cross_arch_std_trend_rho\": -0.3,\n24\t      \"arc_easy_cross_arch_std_trend_p\": 0.55,\n25\t      \"arc_challenge_cross_arch_std_trend_rho\": 0.4,\n26\t      \"arc_challenge_cross_arch_std_trend_p\": 0.6,\n27\t      \"per_example_convergence_any_task\": false,\n28\t      \"cross_task_jaccard_comparison_KW_p\": 0.12,\n29\t      \"n_samples_hellaswag\": 10042,\n30\t      \"n_samples_arc_easy\": 2376,\n31\t      \"n_samples_arc_challenge\": 1172\n32\t    },\n33\t    \"tables\": [\n34\t      {\n35\t        \"name\": \"Table: Per-example divergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\",\n36\t        \"columns\": [\n37\t          \"benchmark\",\n38\t          \"n_samples\",\n39\t          \"mean_jaccard\",\n40\t          \"jaccard_95ci\",\n41\t          \"helped_overlap_pct\",\n42\t          \"hurt_overlap_pct\",\n43\t          \"cross_arch_std_rho\",\n44\t          \"cross_arch_std_p\"\n45\t        ],\n46\t        \"rows\": [\n47\t          [\n48\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n49\t            5153,\n50\t            0.07,\n51\t            \"[0.05, 0.09]\",\n52\t            8.2,\n53\t            6.9,\n54\t            -1.0,\n55\t            0.017\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n59\t            10042,\n60\t            0.08,\n61\t            \"[0.06, 0.10]\",\n62\t            9.1,\n63\t            7.5,\n64\t            0.2,\n65\t            0.75\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n69\t            2376,\n70\t            0.09,\n71\t            \"[0.07, 0.11]\",\n72\t            10.3,\n73\t            8.8,\n74\t            -0.3,\n75\t            0.55\n76\t          ],\n77\t          [\n78\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n79\t            1172,\n80\t            0.07,\n81\t            \"[0.04, 0.10]\",\n82\t            7.8,\n83\t            6.2,\n84\t            0.4,\n85\t            0.6\n86\t          ]\n87\t        ]\n88\t      }\n89\t    ],\n90\t    \"figures\": [],\n91\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-002 的核心价值在于建立对比：convergence 是 task-specific 的 单点现象，但 per-example divergence 是跨 benchmark 的普遍现象。这组数据直接 支持 reframed narrative——论文的核心发现是 attention 导致的 architecture-specific sample specialization，而非 aggregate convergence。即使 convergence claim 完全 失败，Jaccard < 0.12 的跨 benchmark 一致性为 Claim 3 提供了多 benchmark 验证。 不过 cross-task Jaccard 比较的 KW p=0.12 意味着不能 claim divergence 程度有 task dependency——只能说 divergence 存在且 universal。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下，reasoning-heavy tasks 既无 aggregate convergence 也无 per-example convergence。但 Jaccard 值仍然低（0.05-0.12 范围内），说明 per-example divergence 是跨 benchmark 的普遍现象——这实际上 strengthens reframed Claim 3。不同 benchmark 的 Jaccard 无显著差异（KW p=0.12），意味着 architecture-specific sample specialization 是 task-agnostic 的。cross-arch std 趋势在这些 benchmark 上 无方向性（rho 在 -0.3 到 0.4 之间震荡），确认 convergence 确实是 LAMBADA-specific 而非 general。这组数据在 reframed narrative 下反而有用：convergence 是 task-dependent 的（已知），但 per-example divergence 是 universal 的（新发现）。\\n\"\n92\t  },\n93\t  {\n94\t    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n95\t    \"description\": \"提取 3 个架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weight patterns，分析 attention pattern 与 helped/hurt sample identity 的相关性。Worst 档下 correlation < 0.15， attention patterns 无法解释 per-example 差异。\\n\",\n96\t    \"results\": {\n97\t      \"gdn_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.08,\n98\t      \"retnet_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.11,\n99\t      \"hgrn2_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.06,\n100\t      \"max_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.11,\n101\t      \"cross_arch_attn_pattern_similarity\": 0.35,\n102\t      \"attn_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p_gdn\": 0.18,\n103\t      \"attn_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p_retnet\": 0.09,\n104\t      \"attn_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p_hgrn2\": 0.41,\n105\t      \"attn_head_specialization_score\": 0.12,\n106\t      \"position_bias_correlation_with_effect\": 0.05\n107\t    },\n108\t    \"tables\": [\n109\t      {\n110\t        \"name\": \"Table: Attention pattern — per-example effect correlation\",\n111\t        \"columns\": [\n112\t          \"architecture\",\n113\t          \"spearman_rho\",\n114\t          \"p_value\",\n115\t          \"n_samples\",\n116\t          \"attn_entropy_diff_p\"\n117\t        ],\n118\t        \"rows\": [\n119\t          [\n120\t            \"GatedDeltaNet\",\n121\t            0.08,\n122\t            0.065,\n123\t            5153,\n124\t            0.18\n125\t          ],\n126\t          [\n127\t            \"RetNet\",\n128\t            0.11,\n129\t            0.014,\n130\t            5153,\n131\t            0.09\n132\t          ],\n133\t          [\n134\t            \"HGRN2\",\n135\t            0.06,\n136\t            0.182,\n137\t            5153,\n138\t            0.41\n139\t          ]\n140\t        ]\n141\t      },\n142\t      {\n143\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture attention pattern similarity (cosine)\",\n144\t        \"columns\": [\n145\t          \"pair\",\n146\t          \"mean_cosine_sim\",\n147\t          \"std\",\n148\t          \"overlap_top10pct_positions\"\n149\t        ],\n150\t        \"rows\": [\n151\t          [\n152\t            \"GDN-RetNet\",\n153\t            0.38,\n154\t            0.15,\n155\t            0.22\n156\t          ],\n157\t          [\n158\t            \"GDN-HGRN2\",\n159\t            0.31,\n160\t            0.18,\n161\t            0.19\n162\t          ],\n163\t          [\n164\t            \"RetNet-HGRN2\",\n165\t            0.36,\n166\t            0.14,\n167\t            0.21\n168\t          ]\n169\t        ]\n170\t      }\n171\t    ],\n172\t    \"figures\": [],\n173\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-004 是一个 informative negative：attention weight patterns 本身 不能解释 per-example 效应。这并不削弱 Claim 3——反而加强了 \\\"opaque to standard features\\\" 的论述。Surface features 不行（exp-003），perplexity 不行 （exp-003-p2），现在 attention patterns 也不行。Per-example divergence 的来源 可能在 attention 与 recurrent state 的非线性交互中，这超出了 descriptive analysis 的能力范围，诚实地承认并指向 interventional future work（head ablation, activation patching）。论文中 frame 为 \\\"characterization of what does NOT explain the divergence\\\" 而非失败——negative results 在 analysis paper 中有价值。 exp-004 从 \\\"mechanistic evidence\\\" 降级为 \\\"descriptive exploration\\\"，放入 supplementary 或 appendix。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设是 attention patterns 对 per-example 效应无解释力。Correlation < 0.15 的原因有几个层面：(1) attention weight 是 input-dependent 的高维对象， 简单的 aggregated statistics（entropy, max attention, positional bias）丢失了 太多信息，真正的机制可能在 attention 与 recurrent state 的交互中，单独看 attention 不够；(2) helped/hurt 的二分类本身粗糙——attention 可能对 logprob 变化有连续影响但被二值化后信号衰减；(3) h3-1 只有 3 层 attention（每 8 层一层）， 信息瓶颈严重，attention 的角色可能更多是 global routing 而非 sample-specific processing，pattern 差异不映射到 per-example outcome 差异。Cross-arch similarity 0.35 说明不同架构的 attention 做了部分相似的事但不完全相同——既不能说 attention 导致了 convergence（similarity 不够高），也不能说 attention 解释了 divergence （correlation 太低）。\\n\"\n174\t  },\n175\t  {\n176\t    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n177\t    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 和其他来源，寻找额外的 hybrid 架构 （Mamba/Mamba2 hybrids, RWKV hybrids）。Worst 档下无额外架构可用。\\n\",\n178\t    \"results\": {\n179\t      \"additional_architectures_found\": 0,\n180\t      \"n_architectures_total\": 3,\n181\t      \"mamba_hybrid_available\": false,\n182\t      \"rwkv_hybrid_available\": false,\n183\t      \"other_hybrid_available\": false,\n184\t      \"search_sources_checked\": [\n185\t        \"wang_et_al_zoo\",\n186\t        \"huggingface_hub\",\n187\t        \"github_repos\"\n188\t      ]\n189\t    },\n190\t    \"tables\": [],\n191\t    \"figures\": [],\n192\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-005 确认 n=3 是硬约束。Reviewer Concern D (\\\"n=3 too few\\\") 只能 通过 framing 来 mitigate：(1) 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models 的 systematic design，(2) per-example 分析提供 thousands of data points， (3) 这三个架构代表了当前 linear recurrent 家族的主要分支（gated delta, retention, hierarchical gated），(4) 在 limitations 中诚实承认并指向 future work。 对 reframed narrative 影响有限——per-example divergence 的 Jaccard < 0.10 在 3 个架构上已经充分证明了 architecture-specificity。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. (2025) 的 model zoo 专注于 GatedDeltaNet、RetNet、HGRN2 三个 linear recurrent 架构。Mamba/Mamba2 hybrids（如 Jamba）使用不同的 attention integration 策略且没有公开的 systematic ratio sweep（Jamba 只有一个固定配置）。 RWKV-6 hybrids 尚未有公开的 pretrained checkpoints with varying attention ratios。 RecurrentGemma 是 closed-weight。在 worst 档下，即使找到个别 checkpoint，也 缺乏 attention ratio sweep（需要 h0/h3-1/h6-1/h12-1/h24-1 五个配置）， 无法做 convergence 分析。训练新模型超出 GPU budget。n=3 的限制在 paper 中 必须诚实承认为 limitation，但 per-example analysis 的 5153 data points per comparison 部分补偿了架构数量的不足。\\n\"\n193\t  },\n194\t  {\n195\t    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n196\t    \"description\": \"深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 的 non-monotonic rebound。Per-example 比较 340M 与 1.3B 在相同 attention ratio 下的行为差异。Worst 档下 rebound 无清晰解释， 噪声不可排除。\\n\",\n197\t    \"results\": {\n198\t      \"rebound_effect_size_cohens_d\": 0.15,\n199\t      \"rebound_sample_overlap_with_1_3b\": 0.42,\n200\t      \"rebound_explained_by_training_tokens\": \"inconclusive\",\n201\t      \"capacity_hypothesis_p\": 0.28,\n202\t      \"per_example_340m_1_3b_correlation_at_h8\": 0.18,\n203\t      \"rebound_samples_surface_feature_diff_p\": 0.35,\n204\t      \"rebound_magnitude_std\": 0.008,\n205\t      \"noise_floor_permutation_p\": 0.14\n206\t    },\n207\t    \"tables\": [\n208\t      {\n209\t        \"name\": \"Table: 340M rebound characterization\",\n210\t        \"columns\": [\n211\t          \"metric\",\n212\t          \"value\",\n213\t          \"interpretation\"\n214\t        ],\n215\t        \"rows\": [\n216\t          [\n217\t            \"rebound_magnitude_attn8\",\n218\t            0.008,\n219\t            \"cross-arch std increases from 0.015 to 0.023 at h8\"\n220\t          ],\n221\t          [\n222\t            \"cohens_d\",\n223\t            0.15,\n224\t            \"small effect, within noise range\"\n225\t          ],\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"permutation_p\",\n228\t            0.14,\n229\t            \"not significant at any conventional threshold\"\n230\t          ],\n231\t          [\n232\t            \"340m_1.3b_per_example_r\",\n233\t            0.18,\n234\t            \"near-zero per-example correspondence across scales\"\n235\t          ],\n236\t          [\n237\t            \"training_token_ratio\",\n238\t            \"20B vs 100B\",\n239\t            \"5x confound, cannot separate from scale\"\n240\t          ]\n241\t        ]\n242\t      }\n243\t    ],\n244\t    \"figures\": [],\n245\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 Claim 2 (scale-dependent convergence) 几乎完全失效。340M rebound 既不能被解释也不能被确认为真实信号。在 reframed narrative 下，Claim 2 整体 降级为 supplementary observation：\\\"We observe that convergence appears more complete at 1.3B than 340M, but the confound between scale (340M vs 1.3B) and training data (20B vs 100B tokens) prevents causal attribution. The 340M rebound at high attention ratios is not statistically distinguishable from noise (p=0.14).\\\" 这段话放在 supplementary 即可。主论文只需一句话提及 scale 作为 limitation/future work。\\n\\n\\n340M rebound 在 worst 档下无法与噪声区分开，原因：(1) 340M models 用 20B tokens 训练 vs 1.3B 用 100B tokens——training token confound 与 scale confound 完全混淆，无法解缠；(2) rebound effect size 很小（Cohen's d ≈ 0.15），在 permutation test 下 p=0.14，不能排除采样噪声；(3) 340M 与 1.3B 在 h8 的 per-example correlation 很低（0.18），说明两个 scale 的 attention 效应作用于 不同的 sample subsets，但这可能纯粹是因为 340M 容量不足导致的随机差异而非 有意义的 mechanistic difference；(4) surface features 无法区分 rebound samples 与 non-rebound samples（p=0.35）。整体结论：340M rebound 是 noisy observation， 不能支撑 Claim 2 的 \\\"scale is necessary condition\\\" narrative。\\n\"\n246\t  },\n247\t  {\n248\t    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n249\t    \"description\": \"对 LAMBADA 绘制 aggregate convergence 曲线与 per-example divergence 指标的 co-evolution。Worst 档下 convergence 本身被质疑（GDN-excluded 弱化）， bridge 分析的叙事价值降低。\\n\",\n250\t    \"results\": {\n251\t      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_rho\": -0.8,\n252\t      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_p\": 0.1,\n253\t      \"jaccard_vs_attn_ratio_rho\": -0.6,\n254\t      \"jaccard_vs_attn_ratio_p\": 0.28,\n255\t      \"net_effect_asymmetry_trend\": \"weak_negative\",\n256\t      \"gdn_excluded_bridge_rho\": -0.4,\n257\t      \"gdn_excluded_bridge_p\": 0.5\n258\t    },\n259\t    \"tables\": [\n260\t      {\n261\t        \"name\": \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\",\n262\t        \"columns\": [\n263\t          \"attn_ratio\",\n264\t          \"cross_arch_std\",\n265\t          \"mean_pairwise_jaccard\",\n266\t          \"n_helped_union\",\n267\t          \"n_hurt_union\"\n268\t        ],\n269\t        \"rows\": [\n270\t          [\n271\t            \"h0\",\n272\t            0.024,\n273\t            \"N/A (baseline)\",\n274\t            0,\n275\t            0\n276\t          ],\n277\t          [\n278\t            \"h3-1\",\n279\t            0.018,\n280\t            0.09,\n281\t            1436,\n282\t            1505\n283\t          ],\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"h6-1\",\n286\t            0.012,\n287\t            0.08,\n288\t            1512,\n289\t            1580\n290\t          ],\n291\t          [\n292\t            \"h12-1\",\n293\t            0.008,\n294\t            0.07,\n295\t            1590,\n296\t            1648\n297\t          ],\n298\t          [\n299\t            \"h24-1\",\n300\t            0.005,\n301\t            0.06,\n302\t            1650,\n303\t            1710\n304\t          ]\n305\t        ]\n306\t      }\n307\t    ],\n308\t    \"figures\": [],\n309\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-010 的 bridge 分析从论文核心可视化降级为 illustrative/descriptive figure。不做 \\\"convergence and divergence co-evolve\\\" 的统计 claim——只描述观察到的 趋势并注明 underpowered。在 reframed narrative 下，这个图的用途变为展示 per-example divergence 在不同 attention ratios 下的变化（支撑 Claim 3），而非 证明 convergence-divergence 的 mechanistic link。图仍然有价值但降级为 Figure 3 或 4，不再是 Figure 1/2。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，bridge 分析面临两个问题：(1) 全集 convergence-divergence correlation 看似强（rho=-0.8）但 n=5 attention ratios 只有 120 permutations， p=0.10 不显著——这和 exp-008 的 LAMBADA 结果一致，小 n 下 rank correlation 本身 underpowered；(2) 排除 GDN 后 bridge correlation 跌至 rho=-0.4, p=0.50， 说明 co-evolution 的外观部分依赖 GDN 的 confound-driven convergence。 Jaccard 随 attention ratio 增加确实趋向更低（divergence 增加），但 n=5 的 rank correlation 在 p=0.28 不显著。底线：有方向性趋势但统计上不可靠， 不能作为 claim 的支撑证据。在 reframed narrative 下，这个 bridge 分析从 \\\"核心可视化\\\" 降级为 \\\"illustrative figure\\\"——展示现象但不做统计 claim。\\n\"\n310\t  },\n311\t  {\n312\t    \"name\": \"Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\",\n313\t    \"description\": \"在 StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA 上运行 1.3B 全部模型。Worst 档下所有新 benchmark 均无 convergence 信号，LAMBADA 的孤立性被确认。\\n\",\n314\t    \"results\": {\n315\t      \"storycloze_rho\": -0.3,\n316\t      \"storycloze_p\": 0.45,\n317\t      \"storycloze_cross_arch_std_h0\": 0.019,\n318\t      \"storycloze_cross_arch_std_h24\": 0.016,\n319\t      \"storycloze_std_reduction_pct\": 16,\n320\t      \"boolq_rho\": -0.1,\n321\t      \"boolq_p\": 0.85,\n322\t      \"boolq_cross_arch_std_h0\": 0.022,\n323\t      \"boolq_cross_arch_std_h24\": 0.02,\n324\t      \"boolq_std_reduction_pct\": 9,\n325\t      \"copa_rho\": 0.2,\n326\t      \"copa_p\": 0.7,\n327\t      \"copa_cross_arch_std_h0\": 0.031,\n328\t      \"copa_cross_arch_std_h24\": 0.035,\n329\t      \"copa_std_reduction_pct\": -13,\n330\t      \"best_new_rho\": -0.3,\n331\t      \"best_new_p\": 0.45,\n332\t      \"n_new_significant\": 0,\n333\t      \"bh_fdr_total_significant\": 0,\n334\t      \"bonferroni_total_significant\": 0,\n335\t      \"total_benchmarks_tested\": 9,\n336\t      \"lambada_bh_fdr_adj_p_9tests\": 0.15,\n337\t      \"gdn_excluded_storycloze_rho\": -0.1,\n338\t      \"gdn_excluded_boolq_rho\": 0.3,\n339\t      \"gdn_excluded_copa_rho\": 0.5\n340\t    },\n341\t    \"tables\": [\n342\t      {\n343\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture convergence — all benchmarks (1.3B, 9 tests)\",\n344\t        \"columns\": [\n345\t          \"benchmark\",\n346\t          \"task_type\",\n347\t          \"rho\",\n348\t          \"raw_p\",\n349\t          \"bh_fdr_p\",\n350\t          \"bonferroni_p\",\n351\t          \"std_reduction_pct\"\n352\t        ],\n353\t        \"rows\": [\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"LAMBADA\",\n356\t            \"retrieval\",\n357\t            -1.0,\n358\t            0.017,\n359\t            0.15,\n360\t            0.15,\n361\t            79\n362\t          ],\n363\t          [\n364\t            \"StoryCloze\",\n365\t            \"completion\",\n366\t            -0.3,\n367\t            0.45,\n368\t            0.675,\n369\t            1.0,\n370\t            16\n371\t          ],\n372\t          [\n373\t            \"BoolQ\",\n374\t            \"comprehension\",\n375\t            -0.1,\n376\t            0.85,\n377\t            0.956,\n378\t            1.0,\n379\t            9\n380\t          ],\n381\t          [\n382\t            \"COPA\",\n383\t            \"causal\",\n384\t            0.2,\n385\t            0.7,\n386\t            0.9,\n387\t            1.0,\n388\t            -13\n389\t          ],\n390\t          [\n391\t            \"ARC-Easy\",\n392\t            \"mixed\",\n393\t            -0.7,\n394\t            0.233,\n395\t            0.467,\n396\t            1.0,\n397\t            42\n398\t          ],\n399\t          [\n400\t            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n401\t            \"reasoning\",\n402\t            0.6,\n403\t            0.35,\n404\t            0.563,\n405\t            1.0,\n406\t            -18\n407\t          ],\n408\t          [\n409\t            \"HellaSwag\",\n410\t            \"reasoning\",\n411\t            0.3,\n412\t            0.683,\n413\t            0.9,\n414\t            1.0,\n415\t            -8\n416\t          ],\n417\t          [\n418\t            \"WinoGrande\",\n419\t            \"reasoning\",\n420\t            0.1,\n421\t            0.95,\n422\t            0.95,\n423\t            1.0,\n424\t            3\n425\t          ],\n426\t          [\n427\t            \"MMLU\",\n428\t            \"mixed\",\n429\t            -0.7,\n430\t            0.233,\n431\t            0.467,\n432\t            1.0,\n433\t            35\n434\t          ]\n435\t        ]\n436\t      },\n437\t      {\n438\t        \"name\": \"Table: GDN-excluded sensitivity — new benchmarks\",\n439\t        \"columns\": [\n440\t          \"benchmark\",\n441\t          \"full_rho\",\n442\t          \"full_p\",\n443\t          \"gdn_excl_rho\",\n444\t          \"gdn_excl_p\",\n445\t          \"direction\"\n446\t        ],\n447\t        \"rows\": [\n448\t          [\n449\t            \"StoryCloze\",\n450\t            -0.3,\n451\t            0.45,\n452\t            -0.1,\n453\t            0.783,\n454\t            \"WEAKER\"\n455\t          ],\n456\t          [\n457\t            \"BoolQ\",\n458\t            -0.1,\n459\t            0.85,\n460\t            0.3,\n461\t            0.55,\n462\t            \"WEAKER\"\n463\t          ],\n464\t          [\n465\t            \"COPA\",\n466\t            0.2,\n467\t            0.7,\n468\t            0.5,\n469\t            0.45,\n470\t            \"WEAKER\"\n471\t          ]\n472\t        ]\n473\t      }\n474\t    ],\n475\t    \"figures\": [],\n476\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-011 的 worst 档结果是整个项目叙事转折的 trigger。三个关键后果： (1) Convergence claim 彻底死亡——9 个 benchmarks 中 0 个 survive BH-FDR， LAMBADA 自身的 adj-p 从 0.10（6 tests）恶化到 0.15（9 tests），增加 tests 反而 hurt statistical case。 (2) Task-specificity taxonomy 失去了正面 anchor——不再是 \\\"retrieval tasks converge, reasoning tasks don't\\\"，而是 \\\"nothing converges except maybe LAMBADA and that's likely noise or GDN-driven\\\"。 (3) 但 per-example divergence 分析完全不受影响——Jaccard < 0.10 在 LAMBADA 上的发现不依赖 convergence，且如果 exp-002 在新 benchmarks 上也发现低 Jaccard， 那 per-example architecture-specificity 是独立于 convergence 的 robust finding。 论文的 reframe 路径：Title 变为 per-example divergence 论文，LAMBADA convergence 在 discussion 中用 1-2 段提及（\\\"on one retrieval benchmark we observe suggestive but non-significant convergence\\\"），核心贡献完全转向 Claim 3。\\n\\nWorst 档的核心预测：所有新 benchmark ρ > -0.5 且 p > 0.25。原因：(1) StoryCloze 虽然结构类似 LAMBADA（context → completion），但选项是两个完整句子而非单个 token，architectures 的差异在句子级别的 likelihood ranking 上不缩小——attention 帮助的方式更分散，不像 LAMBADA 的单 token retrieval 那样有 focal point； (2) BoolQ 是 passage-based yes/no，本质上是 reading comprehension，更接近 reasoning 而非 pure retrieval，convergence 不出现与 HellaSwag/ARC 一致； (3) COPA 是 causal reasoning，样本量小（400 test + 100 val），noise floor 高， cross-arch std 本身波动大，rho 可以是正的纯粹因为噪声。排除 GDN 后进一步 恶化——StoryCloze rho 从 -0.3 变成 -0.1，证实 GDN 贡献了大部分微弱的趋势。 BH-FDR 在 9 个 tests 下对 LAMBADA 的 adj-p 从 0.10 变成 0.15，LAMBADA 本身 也不再 survive FDR。这是 worst 档最致命的结果：不仅没找到第二个 anchor， 反而因为增加了 test 数量让 LAMBADA 的多重校正更严格。\\n\"\n477\t  }\n478\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96a4463a-edfa-429d-98c4-89aa467fd2ef","uuid":"13d1d7f6-ace3-4bc4-b50e-d9b498f96065","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:16:47.982Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark per-example analysis (task-specificity validation)\",\n    \"description\": \"Re-run lm-eval on 1.3B models with --log_samples for HellaSwag, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge。收集 per-example logprob 数据。在 worst 档下，这些 reasoning-heavy benchmarks 的 per-example 分析不会产生 convergence 信号， 但会为 per-example divergence 分析提供对比组。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_mean\": 0.08,\n      \"hellaswag_pairwise_jaccard_range\": [\n        0.05,\n        0.11\n      ],\n      \"arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_mean\": 0.09,\n      \"arc_easy_pairwise_jaccard_range\": [\n        0.06,\n        0.12\n      ],\n      \"arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_mean\": 0.07,\n      \"arc_challenge_pairwise_jaccard_range\": [\n        0.04,\n        0.1\n      ],\n      \"hellaswag_cross_arch_std_trend_rho\": 0.2,\n      \"hellaswag_cross_arch_std_trend_p\": 0.75,\n      \"arc_easy_cross_arch_std_trend_rho\": -0.3,\n      \"arc_easy_cross_arch_std_trend_p\": 0.55,\n      \"arc_challenge_cross_arch_std_trend_rho\": 0.4,\n      \"arc_challenge_cross_arch_std_trend_p\": 0.6,\n      \"per_example_convergence_any_task\": false,\n      \"cross_task_jaccard_comparison_KW_p\": 0.12,\n      \"n_samples_hellaswag\": 10042,\n      \"n_samples_arc_easy\": 2376,\n      \"n_samples_arc_challenge\": 1172\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Per-example divergence metrics across benchmarks (1.3B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"n_samples\",\n          \"mean_jaccard\",\n          \"jaccard_95ci\",\n          \"helped_overlap_pct\",\n          \"hurt_overlap_pct\",\n          \"cross_arch_std_rho\",\n          \"cross_arch_std_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            5153,\n            0.07,\n            \"[0.05, 0.09]\",\n            8.2,\n            6.9,\n            -1.0,\n            0.017\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            10042,\n            0.08,\n            \"[0.06, 0.10]\",\n            9.1,\n            7.5,\n            0.2,\n            0.75\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            2376,\n            0.09,\n            \"[0.07, 0.11]\",\n            10.3,\n            8.8,\n            -0.3,\n            0.55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            1172,\n            0.07,\n            \"[0.04, 0.10]\",\n            7.8,\n            6.2,\n            0.4,\n            0.6\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-002 的核心价值在于建立对比：convergence 是 task-specific 的 单点现象，但 per-example divergence 是跨 benchmark 的普遍现象。这组数据直接 支持 reframed narrative——论文的核心发现是 attention 导致的 architecture-specific sample specialization，而非 aggregate convergence。即使 convergence claim 完全 失败，Jaccard < 0.12 的跨 benchmark 一致性为 Claim 3 提供了多 benchmark 验证。 不过 cross-task Jaccard 比较的 KW p=0.12 意味着不能 claim divergence 程度有 task dependency——只能说 divergence 存在且 universal。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下，reasoning-heavy tasks 既无 aggregate convergence 也无 per-example convergence。但 Jaccard 值仍然低（0.05-0.12 范围内），说明 per-example divergence 是跨 benchmark 的普遍现象——这实际上 strengthens reframed Claim 3。不同 benchmark 的 Jaccard 无显著差异（KW p=0.12），意味着 architecture-specific sample specialization 是 task-agnostic 的。cross-arch std 趋势在这些 benchmark 上 无方向性（rho 在 -0.3 到 0.4 之间震荡），确认 convergence 确实是 LAMBADA-specific 而非 general。这组数据在 reframed narrative 下反而有用：convergence 是 task-dependent 的（已知），但 per-example divergence 是 universal 的（新发现）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Attention weight extraction and visualization\",\n    \"description\": \"提取 3 个架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weight patterns，分析 attention pattern 与 helped/hurt sample identity 的相关性。Worst 档下 correlation < 0.15， attention patterns 无法解释 per-example 差异。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gdn_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.08,\n      \"retnet_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.11,\n      \"hgrn2_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.06,\n      \"max_attn_effect_correlation\": 0.11,\n      \"cross_arch_attn_pattern_similarity\": 0.35,\n      \"attn_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p_gdn\": 0.18,\n      \"attn_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p_retnet\": 0.09,\n      \"attn_entropy_helped_vs_hurt_p_hgrn2\": 0.41,\n      \"attn_head_specialization_score\": 0.12,\n      \"position_bias_correlation_with_effect\": 0.05\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Attention pattern — per-example effect correlation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"architecture\",\n          \"spearman_rho\",\n          \"p_value\",\n          \"n_samples\",\n          \"attn_entropy_diff_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GatedDeltaNet\",\n            0.08,\n            0.065,\n            5153,\n            0.18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet\",\n            0.11,\n            0.014,\n            5153,\n            0.09\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HGRN2\",\n            0.06,\n            0.182,\n            5153,\n            0.41\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture attention pattern similarity (cosine)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"pair\",\n          \"mean_cosine_sim\",\n          \"std\",\n          \"overlap_top10pct_positions\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GDN-RetNet\",\n            0.38,\n            0.15,\n            0.22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GDN-HGRN2\",\n            0.31,\n            0.18,\n            0.19\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RetNet-HGRN2\",\n            0.36,\n            0.14,\n            0.21\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-004 是一个 informative negative：attention weight patterns 本身 不能解释 per-example 效应。这并不削弱 Claim 3——反而加强了 \\\"opaque to standard features\\\" 的论述。Surface features 不行（exp-003），perplexity 不行 （exp-003-p2），现在 attention patterns 也不行。Per-example divergence 的来源 可能在 attention 与 recurrent state 的非线性交互中，这超出了 descriptive analysis 的能力范围，诚实地承认并指向 interventional future work（head ablation, activation patching）。论文中 frame 为 \\\"characterization of what does NOT explain the divergence\\\" 而非失败——negative results 在 analysis paper 中有价值。 exp-004 从 \\\"mechanistic evidence\\\" 降级为 \\\"descriptive exploration\\\"，放入 supplementary 或 appendix。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心假设是 attention patterns 对 per-example 效应无解释力。Correlation < 0.15 的原因有几个层面：(1) attention weight 是 input-dependent 的高维对象， 简单的 aggregated statistics（entropy, max attention, positional bias）丢失了 太多信息，真正的机制可能在 attention 与 recurrent state 的交互中，单独看 attention 不够；(2) helped/hurt 的二分类本身粗糙——attention 可能对 logprob 变化有连续影响但被二值化后信号衰减；(3) h3-1 只有 3 层 attention（每 8 层一层）， 信息瓶颈严重，attention 的角色可能更多是 global routing 而非 sample-specific processing，pattern 差异不映射到 per-example outcome 差异。Cross-arch similarity 0.35 说明不同架构的 attention 做了部分相似的事但不完全相同——既不能说 attention 导致了 convergence（similarity 不够高），也不能说 attention 解释了 divergence （correlation 太低）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Architecture expansion check\",\n    \"description\": \"搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 和其他来源，寻找额外的 hybrid 架构 （Mamba/Mamba2 hybrids, RWKV hybrids）。Worst 档下无额外架构可用。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"additional_architectures_found\": 0,\n      \"n_architectures_total\": 3,\n      \"mamba_hybrid_available\": false,\n      \"rwkv_hybrid_available\": false,\n      \"other_hybrid_available\": false,\n      \"search_sources_checked\": [\n        \"wang_et_al_zoo\",\n        \"huggingface_hub\",\n        \"github_repos\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-005 确认 n=3 是硬约束。Reviewer Concern D (\\\"n=3 too few\\\") 只能 通过 framing 来 mitigate：(1) 3 architectures × 5 ratios × 2 scales = 30 models 的 systematic design，(2) per-example 分析提供 thousands of data points， (3) 这三个架构代表了当前 linear recurrent 家族的主要分支（gated delta, retention, hierarchical gated），(4) 在 limitations 中诚实承认并指向 future work。 对 reframed narrative 影响有限——per-example divergence 的 Jaccard < 0.10 在 3 个架构上已经充分证明了 architecture-specificity。\\n\\n\\nWang et al. (2025) 的 model zoo 专注于 GatedDeltaNet、RetNet、HGRN2 三个 linear recurrent 架构。Mamba/Mamba2 hybrids（如 Jamba）使用不同的 attention integration 策略且没有公开的 systematic ratio sweep（Jamba 只有一个固定配置）。 RWKV-6 hybrids 尚未有公开的 pretrained checkpoints with varying attention ratios。 RecurrentGemma 是 closed-weight。在 worst 档下，即使找到个别 checkpoint，也 缺乏 attention ratio sweep（需要 h0/h3-1/h6-1/h12-1/h24-1 五个配置）， 无法做 convergence 分析。训练新模型超出 GPU budget。n=3 的限制在 paper 中 必须诚实承认为 limitation，但 per-example analysis 的 5153 data points per comparison 部分补偿了架构数量的不足。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"340M rebound mechanism analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"深入分析 340M 在 attn=8 的 non-monotonic rebound。Per-example 比较 340M 与 1.3B 在相同 attention ratio 下的行为差异。Worst 档下 rebound 无清晰解释， 噪声不可排除。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rebound_effect_size_cohens_d\": 0.15,\n      \"rebound_sample_overlap_with_1_3b\": 0.42,\n      \"rebound_explained_by_training_tokens\": \"inconclusive\",\n      \"capacity_hypothesis_p\": 0.28,\n      \"per_example_340m_1_3b_correlation_at_h8\": 0.18,\n      \"rebound_samples_surface_feature_diff_p\": 0.35,\n      \"rebound_magnitude_std\": 0.008,\n      \"noise_floor_permutation_p\": 0.14\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 340M rebound characterization\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"rebound_magnitude_attn8\",\n            0.008,\n            \"cross-arch std increases from 0.015 to 0.023 at h8\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cohens_d\",\n            0.15,\n            \"small effect, within noise range\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"permutation_p\",\n            0.14,\n            \"not significant at any conventional threshold\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"340m_1.3b_per_example_r\",\n            0.18,\n            \"near-zero per-example correspondence across scales\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"training_token_ratio\",\n            \"20B vs 100B\",\n            \"5x confound, cannot separate from scale\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 Claim 2 (scale-dependent convergence) 几乎完全失效。340M rebound 既不能被解释也不能被确认为真实信号。在 reframed narrative 下，Claim 2 整体 降级为 supplementary observation：\\\"We observe that convergence appears more complete at 1.3B than 340M, but the confound between scale (340M vs 1.3B) and training data (20B vs 100B tokens) prevents causal attribution. The 340M rebound at high attention ratios is not statistically distinguishable from noise (p=0.14).\\\" 这段话放在 supplementary 即可。主论文只需一句话提及 scale 作为 limitation/future work。\\n\\n\\n340M rebound 在 worst 档下无法与噪声区分开，原因：(1) 340M models 用 20B tokens 训练 vs 1.3B 用 100B tokens——training token confound 与 scale confound 完全混淆，无法解缠；(2) rebound effect size 很小（Cohen's d ≈ 0.15），在 permutation test 下 p=0.14，不能排除采样噪声；(3) 340M 与 1.3B 在 h8 的 per-example correlation 很低（0.18），说明两个 scale 的 attention 效应作用于 不同的 sample subsets，但这可能纯粹是因为 340M 容量不足导致的随机差异而非 有意义的 mechanistic difference；(4) surface features 无法区分 rebound samples 与 non-rebound samples（p=0.35）。整体结论：340M rebound 是 noisy observation， 不能支撑 Claim 2 的 \\\"scale is necessary condition\\\" narrative。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"对 LAMBADA 绘制 aggregate convergence 曲线与 per-example divergence 指标的 co-evolution。Worst 档下 convergence 本身被质疑（GDN-excluded 弱化）， bridge 分析的叙事价值降低。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_rho\": -0.8,\n      \"convergence_divergence_correlation_p\": 0.1,\n      \"jaccard_vs_attn_ratio_rho\": -0.6,\n      \"jaccard_vs_attn_ratio_p\": 0.28,\n      \"net_effect_asymmetry_trend\": \"weak_negative\",\n      \"gdn_excluded_bridge_rho\": -0.4,\n      \"gdn_excluded_bridge_p\": 0.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution (LAMBADA, 1.3B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"attn_ratio\",\n          \"cross_arch_std\",\n          \"mean_pairwise_jaccard\",\n          \"n_helped_union\",\n          \"n_hurt_union\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"h0\",\n            0.024,\n            \"N/A (baseline)\",\n            0,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h3-1\",\n            0.018,\n            0.09,\n            1436,\n            1505\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h6-1\",\n            0.012,\n            0.08,\n            1512,\n            1580\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h12-1\",\n            0.008,\n            0.07,\n            1590,\n            1648\n          ],\n          [\n            \"h24-1\",\n            0.005,\n            0.06,\n            1650,\n            1710\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst 档下 exp-010 的 bridge 分析从论文核心可视化降级为 illustrative/descriptive figure。不做 \\\"convergence and divergence co-evolve\\\" 的统计 claim——只描述观察到的 趋势并注明 underpowered。在 reframed narrative 下，这个图的用途变为展示 per-example divergence 在不同 attention ratios 下的变化（支撑 Claim 3），而非 证明 convergence-divergence 的 mechanistic link。图仍然有价值但降级为 Figure 3 或 4，不再是 Figure 1/2。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，bridge 分析面临两个问题：(1) 全集 convergence-divergence correlation 看似强（rho=-0.8）但 n=5 attention ratios 只有 120 permutations， p=0.10 不显著——这和 exp-008 的 LAMBADA 结果一致，小 n 下 rank correlation 本身 underpowered；(2) 排除 GDN 后 bridge correlation 跌至 rho=-0.4, p=0.50， 说明 co-evolution 的外观部分依赖 GDN 的 confound-driven convergence。 Jaccard 随 attention ratio 增加确实趋向更低（divergence 增加），但 n=5 的 rank correlation 在 p=0.28 不显著。底线：有方向性趋势但统计上不可靠， 不能作为 claim 的支撑证据。在 reframed narrative 下，这个 bridge 分析从 \\\"核心可视化\\\" 降级为 \\\"illustrative figure\\\"——展示现象但不做统计 claim。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\",\n    \"description\": \"在 StoryCloze, BoolQ, COPA 上运行 1.3B 全部模型。Worst 档下所有新 benchmark 均无 convergence 信号，LAMBADA 的孤立性被确认。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"storycloze_rho\": -0.3,\n      \"storycloze_p\": 0.45,\n      \"storycloze_cross_arch_std_h0\": 0.019,\n      \"storycloze_cross_arch_std_h24\": 0.016,\n      \"storycloze_std_reduction_pct\": 16,\n      \"boolq_rho\": -0.1,\n      \"boolq_p\": 0.85,\n      \"boolq_cross_arch_std_h0\": 0.022,\n      \"boolq_cross_arch_std_h24\": 0.02,\n      \"boolq_std_reduction_pct\": 9,\n      \"copa_rho\": 0.2,\n      \"copa_p\": 0.7,\n      \"copa_cross_arch_std_h0\": 0.031,\n      \"copa_cross_arch_std_h24\": 0.035,\n      \"copa_std_reduction_pct\": -13,\n      \"best_new_rho\": -0.3,\n      \"best_new_p\": 0.45,\n      \"n_new_significant\": 0,\n      \"bh_fdr_total_significant\": 0,\n      \"bonferroni_total_significant\": 0,\n      \"total_benchmarks_tested\": 9,\n      \"lambada_bh_fdr_adj_p_9tests\": 0.15,\n      \"gdn_excluded_storycloze_rho\": -0.1,\n      \"gdn_excluded_boolq_rho\": 0.3,\n      \"gdn_excluded_copa_rho\": 0.5\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-architecture convergence — all benchmarks (1.3B, 9 tests)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"task_type\",\n          \"rho\",\n          \"raw_p\",\n          \"bh_fdr_p\",\n          \"bonferroni_p\",\n          \"std_reduction_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LAMBADA\",\n            \"retrieval\",\n            -1.0,\n            0.017,\n            0.15,\n            0.15,\n            79\n          ],\n          [\n            \"StoryCloze\",\n            \"completion\",\n            -0.3,\n            0.45,\n            0.675,\n            1.0,\n            16\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BoolQ\",\n            \"comprehension\",\n            -0.1,\n            0.85,\n            0.956,\n            1.0,\n            9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"COPA\",\n            \"causal\",\n            0.2,\n            0.7,\n            0.9,\n            1.0,\n            -13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Easy\",\n            \"mixed\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.233,\n            0.467,\n            1.0,\n            42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            \"reasoning\",\n            0.6,\n            0.35,\n            0.563,\n            1.0,\n            -18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"reasoning\",\n            0.3,\n            0.683,\n            0.9,\n            1.0,\n            -8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"WinoGrande\",\n            \"reasoning\",\n            0.1,\n            0.95,\n            0.95,\n            1.0,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"mixed\",\n            -0.7,\n            0.233,\n            0.467,\n            1.0,\n            35\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GDN-excluded sensitivity — new benchmarks\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"benchmark\",\n          \"full_rho\",\n          \"full_p\",\n          \"gdn_excl_rho\",\n          \"gdn_excl_p\",\n          \"direction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"StoryCloze\",\n            -0.3,\n            0.45,\n            -0.1,\n            0.783,\n            \"WEAKER\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BoolQ\",\n            -0.1,\n            0.85,\n            0.3,\n            0.55,\n            \"WEAKER\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"COPA\",\n            0.2,\n            0.7,\n            0.5,\n            0.45,\n            \"WEAKER\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-011 的 worst 档结果是整个项目叙事转折的 trigger。三个关键后果： (1) Convergence claim 彻底死亡——9 个 benchmarks 中 0 个 survive BH-FDR， LAMBADA 自身的 adj-p 从 0.10（6 tests）恶化到 0.15（9 tests），增加 tests 反而 hurt statistical case。 (2) Task-specificity taxonomy 失去了正面 anchor——不再是 \\\"retrieval tasks converge, reasoning tasks don't\\\"，而是 \\\"nothing converges except maybe LAMBADA and that's likely noise or GDN-driven\\\"。 (3) 但 per-example divergence 分析完全不受影响——Jaccard < 0.10 在 LAMBADA 上的发现不依赖 convergence，且如果 exp-002 在新 benchmarks 上也发现低 Jaccard， 那 per-example architecture-specificity 是独立于 convergence 的 robust finding。 论文的 reframe 路径：Title 变为 per-example divergence 论文，LAMBADA convergence 在 discussion 中用 1-2 段提及（\\\"on one retrieval benchmark we observe suggestive but non-significant convergence\\\"），核心贡献完全转向 Claim 3。\\n\\nWorst 档的核心预测：所有新 benchmark ρ > -0.5 且 p > 0.25。原因：(1) StoryCloze 虽然结构类似 LAMBADA（context → completion），但选项是两个完整句子而非单个 token，architectures 的差异在句子级别的 likelihood ranking 上不缩小——attention 帮助的方式更分散，不像 LAMBADA 的单 token retrieval 那样有 focal point； (2) BoolQ 是 passage-based yes/no，本质上是 reading comprehension，更接近 reasoning 而非 pure retrieval，convergence 不出现与 HellaSwag/ARC 一致； (3) COPA 是 causal reasoning，样本量小（400 test + 100 val），noise floor 高， cross-arch std 本身波动大，rho 可以是正的纯粹因为噪声。排除 GDN 后进一步 恶化——StoryCloze rho 从 -0.3 变成 -0.1，证实 GDN 贡献了大部分微弱的趋势。 BH-FDR 在 9 个 tests 下对 LAMBADA 的 adj-p 从 0.10 变成 0.15，LAMBADA 本身 也不再 survive FDR。这是 worst 档最致命的结果：不仅没找到第二个 anchor， 反而因为增加了 test 数量让 LAMBADA 的多重校正更严格。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":478,"startLine":1,"totalLines":478}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015iwaPLhxrnB7YRW4Xivsdo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of both the experimental data and the paper framing. Let me also read the paper-writing-norms skill for quality guidance, and check the LaTeX template requirements.\n\nLet me now write the paper. The key points from the narrative guidance:\n\n1. Drop convergence as main claim. Reframe as \"Per-example behavioral divergence in hybrid recurrent architectures — attention induces architecture-specific sample specialization\"\n2. LAMBADA convergence → discussion, single-task observation\n3. Claim 2 (scale) → supplementary entirely\n4. Core contribution = Claim 3: (a) Jaccard < 0.10 architecture-specificity, (b) cross-arch KW p=0.0005 structured non-random, (c) surface features + perplexity can't explain\n\n\n5. The practical angle is that practitioners need to understand how attention mechanisms create divergent per-example behaviors across different architectures, which is crucial for hybrid architecture selection\n6. I'm targeting EMNLP Findings, so I need to build out a solid related work section with 20+ references and frame this through the lens of underspecification and per-example characterization\n7. The experiments I'll cover are the multi-benchmark per-example divergence analysis, attention weight extraction and cross-architecture similarity patterns, the architecture expansion validation, and the 340M rebound mechanism for supplementary material.\n\nNow I'm planning the paper structure carefully—I need to pull all the actual numbers from the experiment data without inventing anything, organize it with standard sections including a substantial related work, and make sure the per-example divergence is the centerpiece while pushing convergence analysis into the discussion. The scale analysis goes to supplementary, and I'll include all the relevant tables from 